      "notes": "Pure Go codecs and existing guarded archive sink; exact entry identity or explicit refusal, never TrimSpace renaming. Refuse traversal, escaping symlinks, bombs, unsupported metadata. Existing extract caps remain500 entries/50MiB; recursive mutation10k/100MiB is separate. tar -cj uses pinned dsnet bzip2 writer; standard library only decodes. gzip/gunzip replace through recovery, zcat always stream; stdin - supported. tar short mode bundles -xzf/-tf accepted; repeated modes/codecs reject. -v prints member names for -c and -x and a GNU long listing for -t; member operands select named entries and the entries beneath named directories. tar -J/--xz and --zstd read and write .tar.xz and .tar.zst (xz dictionaries above 64 MiB and zstd windows above 8 MiB refuse); extraction and listing sniff all four codecs. -a picks the codec from the archive suffix. --exclude PATTERN, -X FILE lines and --exclude-vcs are globs whose * matches /, tested against every run of whole name components; an excluded directory is not descended. -T FILE adds one name per line. Exclusion and name files are read through read authority; the archive never contains itself.",
